    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0299" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-15T16:00:00-05:00">February 15, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Department’s telegram No. 17, February 12, 6 p.m. The Dominican Foreign
                    Minister said that formal instructions to Pastoriza<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d367-f1"/> have not yet been sent presumably because of the
                    General’s absence on a high seas cruise, but reaffirmed in the most positive way
                    Dominican adherence to extending the powers of the Neutrality Committee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d367-f1" n="44" xml:id="d367-f1-content">
                <p>Andrés Pastoriza, Dominican Minister in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
